    Clerk: make economy-resources smoke hermetic under host load
    
    The full run-all suite itself raises host load above the Act 29 watch threshold
    (per_cpu uses load5), so the "healthy" fixture intermittently reports overall=watch
    and aborts the suite under set -e, blocking Act 31 landing of the Act 32
    codification. This is environmental, not a resource-policy defect.
    
    Add VICHE_ECONOMY_LOAD_OVERRIDE JSON to economy-resources.py, matching the existing
    NOW/FS/CGROUP test overrides, and set a low static load in the smoke test. Real
    operation is unchanged: the override is only read when the env var is present.
    Verified economy-resources-smoke and full tests/run-all.sh green.

